<p class="eyebrow">NATHAN AI 🚀 → TABOR ROOT → TABOR 1–2–3 FACTORY → ONE</p>
<h1>The Architecture Infrastructure Index</h1>
<p class="intro">21 critical software frameworks, hardware systems and computational interfaces. The original author-supplied <strong>Function</strong> and <strong>Rule</strong> entries are retained. No hardware or network deployment is implied by this index.</p>
<div class="statrow"><div class="stat"><strong>7</strong><span>Software architectures</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>7</strong><span>Hardware arrays</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>7</strong><span>Connectivity interfaces</span></div></div>
<div class="filters"><label for="category">Section</label><select id="category"><option value="all">All 21</option><option value="software">1 — Software</option><option value="hardware">2 — Hardware</option><option value="connectivity">3 — Connectivity</option></select><label for="query">Search</label><input id="query" type="search" placeholder="Name, function or rule" aria-label="Search all 21 records"><button id="export">Export this index</button></div>
<p id="results-count" role="status" class="small">21 records</p><div id="cards" class="cards"></div>
<section class="panel"><h2>Accords, governance and deployment boundary</h2><p>This index is a sibling infrastructure layer alongside the Tabor Accords (<code>NT-ACC-001</code>; <code>BASE:NT-ADDED-087</code>) inside the existing Nathan AI / ONE architecture. Consent, protection, provenance and due process are governing requirements—not claims of unrestricted control over operating systems, networks, devices or third-party data.</p><p class="small">Separate editorial notes in <a href="./README.md">README.md</a> flag overstatements on Git immutability, Kubernetes uptime, portable containers, quantum advantage and the 6G standardization timeline. Original source wording remains unchanged.</p></section>
<footer>Additive, local-first reference browser. No telemetry, login, device probing, system modifications, or external API calls. Owner-written content is distinct from verification and operational status.</footer>
</main><script src="./records.js"></script><script>(function(){"use strict";const idx=window.NathanInfrastructureIndex;const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);function t(tag,text,cls){const n=document.createElement(tag);n.textContent=text;if(cls)n.className=cls;return n}function display(s){return s.replace(/^&#x53;/,"S")}function draw(){const cat=$("category").value,q=$("query").value.trim().toLocaleLowerCase();const matches=idx.records.filter(r=>(cat==="all"||r.category===cat)&&[r.name,r.epithet,r.sourceFunction,r.sourceRule].join(" ").toLocaleLowerCase().includes(q));const target=$("cards");target.replaceChildren();for(const r of matches){const card=t("article","","card");card.append(t("div",String(r.number).padStart(2,"0")+" · "+r.category.toUpperCase(),"num"),t("h3",r.name),t("p",r.epithet,"epithet"));const dl=document.createElement("dl");for(const [k,v] of [["The Function",r.sourceFunction],["The Rule",r.sourceRule]]){dl.append(t("dt",k),t("dd",display(v)))}card.append(dl);target.append(card)}$("results-count").textContent=matches.length+" of "+idx.records.length+" records";} $("category").addEventListener("change",draw);$("query").addEventListener("input",draw);$("export").addEventListener("click",()=>{const bytes=JSON.stringify({id:idx.id,version:idx.version,categories:idx.categories,records:idx.records},null,2);const u=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([bytes],{type:"application/json"}));const a=document.createElement("a");a.href=u;a.download="Nathan_AI_Infrastructure_Index_21.json";document.body.append(a);a.click();a.remove();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(u),500)});draw()})();</script>
</body></html>